      "textEn": "473\nThis is the nature of a child. That's what it is here. Like children, the saintly men entered all six halls of the palace.\nAnd no one stopped them, therefore, when they tried to enter the seventh gate,\nand they were refused by the gatekeepers who stopped them with their sticks, then naturally they became extremely\nangry and sad. A normal child would have shouted, but these were not normal children, therefore,\nthey immediately prepared to punish the gatekeepers, because these gatekeepers had committed a very big crime.\nThey had committed a great crime. Even today in India, no saint is ever stopped from entering anyone's door.\nTanvikshya Vatarashanamchaturah Kumaran\nVruddhandashardhayaso Viditatmatatvan |\nVetrena Chakshalayataamatdarhanastau\nTejo Vihasya Bhagavatpratikulashilau. 30>. Meaning of the word\n\nAH - to them; Vikshay- seeing; Vaat- rashnan- naked; Chatur- four; Kumaran- children; Vriddhan- quite old;\nDashan- half - five years; Vayasah- seeming of age; Vidit- had experienced; Atm- of the self; Tat- truth;\nVetren- with sticks; Cha- also; Askhalyataam- refused; A- not expecting such; Tau- both of them\nDoorkeepers; Tejah- Ya; Vihasya- without regard to etiquette; Bhagavat- unfavorable- Shilau - those who cause God to be angry\nLL with such nature\n\nFour children, sages, Those who had nothing besides the atmosphere to cover their bodies,\nwere appearing to be five years old, although they were the oldest of all living beings, and\nthey had attained the realization of the truth of the soul. But when the gatekeepers, whose nature\nGod was not at all interested; when he saw these sages, he mocked their glory.\nWhile mocking, he blocked their path with his sticks; although these sages were not worthy of such treatment from his hands. Meaning: The four sages were the first born sons of Brahma. Therefore, Shiva, along with all other beings, later\nwere born as beings, therefore they are smaller than the four Kumaras. Although they looked like five-year-old children,\nand were wandering naked, but they were older than all other beings and they had attained self-\nrealization on. Such saints were not to be prevented from entering the kingdom of Vaikuntha,\nbut coincidentally the gatekeepers objected to their entry. This was not appropriate. Bhagwan"
