      "textEn": "48]\nMeaning of the word\n\nTesham--of the four princes; Iti--in this way; Eritam--uttered; Ubhau--both gatekeepers; Avadharya--understanding; Ghoramu--\nTerrible; Tam--that; Brahma-dandamu--the curse of a Brahmin; Anivaranam--which cannot be averted; Astra-pugai:--by some kind of weapon; Sadyah--immediately; Hareh--of the Lord; Anucharau--devotees; Uru-atyadhika--extremely; Bibhyat:--Became frightened; Tat-pada-grahaau --Holding their feet; Aptatam --Fell; Ati-katrena --In excessive worry.\n\nWhen the gatekeepers of Vaikuntha Loka, who were truly devotees of the Lord, saw that they\nwere about to be cursed by the Brahmins, they immediately became very frightened and, in excessive worry,\nFell at the feet of the Brahmins, because the curse of a Brahmin cannot be removed in any way\nby a weapon. Meaning: Although, coincidentally, the gatekeepers had mistakenly prevented the Brahmins from entering the gate of Vaikuntha,\nthey immediately realized the seriousness of the curse.\nCrimes are of many types,\nBut the biggest crime is to insult a devotee of God. Because the gatekeepers were also devotees of the Lord, therefore,\nthey realized their mistake, and when the four princes were about to curse them, they became frightened\nand fled. Those who are always engaged in the divine, with their bodies and minds,\nWho do not get even a little bit of the divine's joy.\nThey are not free from remorse, and they are not free from the memory of the divine.\nThey are deluded, and they are neither high nor low. 36). Meaning of the word\n\nBhuyat-Esa hi ho; Aghoni-- for the sinner; Bhagavadhih-- by you; Akari-- done; Dandah-- punishment; Yah-who;\nNau-in our relation; Hareet-destroying; Sur-Hellenam-disobeying the great gods; Api-certainly;\nAshosh-immense; Ma-not; Vah-your; Anutap-regret; Kalya-little by little; Bhagavat-of God; Smriti-\nGhnah-destroying the power of memory; Mohah-delusion; Bhaveet-may; Iha-here; Foolish life-womb; Tu-but; Nau-both of us;\nVrajatoh-going; Adha-down; down the material world L\nAfter being cursed by the sages, the gatekeepers said: It was right that you punished us for disrespecting you\nlike sages. But our prayer is that our regrets\nBut because of your mercy, we should not be tempted by forgetting God at that time when we are going down-\nGoing down. Meaning: No matter how severe the punishment, a devotee can bear it, but to make God suffer"
